{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1045","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I. Palindrome Pairs"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After learning a lot about space exploration, a little girl named Ana wants to change the subject."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ana is a girl who loves palindromes (string that can be read the same backwards as forward). She has learned how to check for a given string whether it's a palindrome or not, but soon she grew tired of this problem, so she came up with a more interesting one and she needs your help to solve it:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of strings which consist of only small letters of the alphabet. Your task is to find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"how many"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" palindrome pairs are there in the array. A palindrome pair is a pair of strings such that the following condition holds: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at least one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of the concatenation of the two strings is a palindrome. In other words, if you have two strings, let's say \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and you concatenate them into \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aababcac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", we have to check if there exists a permutation of this new string such that it is a palindrome (in this case there exists the permutation \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aabccbaa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two pairs are considered different if the strings are located on "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different indices"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The pair of strings with indices $$$(i,j)$$$ is considered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the same"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" as the pair $$$(j,i)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a positive integer $$$N$$$ ($$$1 \\le N \\le 100\\,000$$$), representing the length of the input array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Eacg of the next $$$N$$$ lines contains a string (consisting of lowercase English letters from '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' to '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"') — an element of the input array. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The total number of characters in the input array will be less than $$$1\\,000\\,000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output one number, representing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"how many palindrome pairs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" there are in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\naa\nbb\ncd\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\naab\nabcac\ndffe\ned\naa\naade\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$+$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\to$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$+$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$=$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aababcac